    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Komal and tivra",
      "body": "**Komal** means lowered. Komal Re, komal Ga, komal Dha and komal Ni each sit one key below Re, Ga, Dha and Ni.\n\n**Tivra** means raised. Tivra Ma sits one key above Ma.\n\nSa and Pa never change. With Sa on C, the five black keys are komal Re, komal Ga, tivra Ma, komal Dha and komal Ni.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        60,
        61,
        62,
        63,
        64,
        65,
        66,
        67,
        68,
        69,
        70,
        71,
        72
      ],
